Thanks [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] - responses are below.

{quote}It seems that adding information about collecting Tax ID numbers may be confusing because we do not necessarily will collect this information. Another problem we have here is mentioning Modash - we should not add information about third parties if this is not strictly necessary and we don’t know whether Modash will be relevant for all CCs.{quote}

Even if we are only collecting Tax ID for some of these individuals, we should still mention this in the privacy notice. Privacy notices are not tailored documents that apply on a per-individual basis - they are intended to cover a wide range of individuals (whether represented by a legal entity or not). If Modash is relevant for even some of the users, we should leave it in. That is why I deliberately drafted it as “Bolt +*may*+ share your personal data with…”

{quote}Do you think that privacy notice is necessary for those with whom we will be signing an agreement if in the agreement we will explain what data we will collect and to whom we will forward it to? I understand from your message that privacy notice serves as a source of general information about data processing, but does this information necessarily need to be contained in the privacy notice or information provided in the agreement can also be sufficient?{quote}

It should be contained in the privacy notice. The privacy notice contains information which an agreement would not (e.g., legal basis, data subject rights etc.).

{quote}CC with whom we will sign an agreement for services will act as supplier. I do not recall that we have a separate privacy notice for our agreements with suppliers and we normally rely on data protection clauses stated in the agreement.{quote}

Privacy notices are only needed to inform individuals about personal data processing, rather than legal entities. Where a supplier is a legal entity, I can understand why we would not be relying on a privacy notice. However, I understand that we will be contracting with some of these CCs as individuals, which necessitates a privacy notice.

Happy to discuss over a call if easier.

